      "dcterms:title": "Asymptotics of the quantum invariants for surgeries on the figure 8 knot",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "University of Aarhus, Building 530, Ny Munkegade, 8000 Aarhus, Denmark"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20181025",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0506456",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We investigate the Reshetikhin–Turaev invariants associated to SU(2) for the 3– manifolds M obtained by doing any rational surgery along the ﬁgure 8 knot. In partic- ular, we express these invariants in terms of certain complex double contour integrals. These integral formulae allow us to propose a formula for the leading asymptotics of the invariants in the limit of large quantum level. We analyze this expression using the saddle point method. We construct a certain surjection from the set of stationary points for the relevant phase functions onto the space of conjugacy classes of nonabelian SL(2, C)–representations of the fundamental group of M and prove that the values of these phase functions at the relevant stationary points equals the classical Chern–Simons invariants of the corresponding ﬂat SU(2)–connections. Our ﬁndings are in agreement with the asymptotic expansion conjecture. Moreover, we calculate the leading asymp- totics of the colored Jones polynomial of the ﬁgure 8 knot following Kashaev [14]. This leads to a slightly ﬁner asymptotic description of the invariant than predicted by the volume conjecture [24].",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-0506456v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-0506456v1"
    }
  ]
}
